tgenfunc19.pp	gap: WALL MOVED 2026-09-08 at compiler d1d78434de8c, and the row now COMPILES AND LINKS -- it exits rc=1 at `if specialize DoTest<TTest> <> 2 then Halt(1)`. THE SPLICE-POSITION WALL IS GONE: the specialized body used to land at the end of the uses clause, ahead of the program's own type section, so `T` substituted by the program-declared TTest2 read `undefined variable (TTest2)`; bodies are queued now (PendFunc*) and spliced where the declaration section ENDS. WHAT IS LEFT is a class-HELPER rule, and the previous reason here denied exactly that -- it said the helper rule "was already carved out and was never this row's wall", which was TRUE about the wall it measured and FALSE about the file: the helper rule was the NEXT wall, standing behind it, and a wall behind a wall reads as no wall. `T.Test` in the template body resolves to TTest's own class function (1) where fpc applies TTestHelper, declared in the TEMPLATE'S OWN UNIT ten lines above it (2). PRE-EXISTING, proved by stash-and-rebuild at cd2d264c72df. The OTHER row is already correct and constrains the fix: DoTest<TTest2>, whose helper is declared in the SPECIALIZING program, answers 3 as fpc does -- widening helper lookup at the specialization site would flip it to 4 silently. bug-p-a-generic-routine-body-does-not-see-its-own-units-class-helper
