toperator91.pp	gap: THE DECLARATION HALF IS DONE FOR EXPLICIT CASTS (2026-09-07, compiler b2784460a6a5) and the old reason's COSTING was wrong in a way worth keeping. It said the declaration half needs a ProcRetStrCap column and is 'contained', and that the use-site half is optional idiosyncrasy. Built the column -- and the declaration half ALONE would have been a silent-wrong-answer generator, because the use-site lookup keys on the result KIND too, so three operators would have registered and every cast would have reached the first. The two are one change or neither. Done: `class operator Explicit(...): String[80]` / `: String[90]` / `: ShortString` now all declare, and `TString80(t)` / `TString90(t)` reach their OWN operator, matching fpc 3.2.2 exactly; a destination with no matching capacity falls back to the generic ShortString one. Fixture test/test_conversion_operator_result_capacity_is_part_of_its_identity.pas. WHAT BLOCKS THIS ROW NOW IS THE IMPLICIT TRIO, and it is a DIFFERENT question from the one the old reason named. Capacity is deliberately confined to OPK_EXPLICIT: measured 2026-09-07, fpc resolves every IMPLICIT assignment to the GENERIC conversion and, where none is declared, refuses at the STORE (`Incompatible types: got "TTest" expected "TString80"`, toperator92/95) rather than choosing among the sized ones. So capacity has nothing to decide there, and splitting Implicit by it made toperator92/95 accepted-invalid -- both declarations register, the destination-agnostic store-permission check says a conversion exists, the rewrite matches none and the store goes through RAW. TO BURN THIS ROW: accept the Implicit declarations (fpc does) and move our diagnostic from the DECLARATION to the STORE, which is where fpc raises it. That is a real, contained next step and it is not the ranking emulation the old reason warned off -- fpc's `ShortString Implicit` SIX TIMES ranking stays out of scope and is still what would remain after it.
toperator94.pp	gap: same family as toperator91 -- see that row, whose reason and costing were both corrected 2026-09-07. The EXPLICIT half of the coarseness is fixed (result capacity is part of a conversion's identity now); this row is the objfpc `class operator :=` spelling, i.e. the IMPLICIT side, which is exactly the half deliberately left keyed on the result KIND because fpc gives implicit assignment no capacity discrimination at all. Blocked on the same single step: move the duplicate diagnostic from the declaration to the store.
